subject: docs(research): Finding #17 — published 9router@0.5.109 package audit

Read-only tarball inspection of the published 0.5.109 package (backlog #5).

Findings:

- The runtime is the compiled .next-cli-build/ standalone bundle; the package/app/src/

  tree is vestigial (imports files that do not ship).

- Only migration 001 ships. 002/003/004/005 are absent (bundle was cut from a

  different checkout — outputFileTracingRoot=/Users/Working/router4 — despite

  those migrations being committed 11+ hours before the publish timestamp).

- No rate limiter of any kind ships (neither TCP-layer nor middleware-layer).

- CHANGELOG.md ends at v0.5.95; versions 0.5.99/0.5.104/0.5.109 have no entries.

Recommendation: do NOT upgrade mini2 via npm i -g 9router@0.5.109 (it trades

the RSC-429 bug for a security regression — no rate limiting at all). Build

from repo HEAD instead. FK risk from Findings #2/#14 is cleared: 002 neither

ships in 0.5.109 nor is registered in repo HEAD.

Also documents resolutions for Findings #12/#13/#15/#16 and marks backlog

items #5-#12 resolved.

